  "name": "Example: Determining the Amplitude of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function",
  "problem": "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x) = -2\\sin\\left(x-\\dfrac\\pi 3\\right) + 1?$",
  "worked_solution": "Given a function in the form $f(x)= A\\sin(Bx +C) + D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-2.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=2.$",
